Subject: [PATCH 2/2] dsh: a list that reads empty right after a write is
 reread before one is written (#5782)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The half stevenpisces' machine lost through was not the again path's: the
list read as its comment head and no entries, magpie filled its route in
under a start that still named one of its models, and the fresh generation
went back as head plus those two entries — the user's 51 lines gone, the
half matching 4 of them. The model-set path said nothing as it did.

dshSettledRead is the read a writer's write cannot hide behind, the same
shape dshRouteAgainSaid's gate uses, on every path that generates fresh
into a list that read empty: the model set (dshSetFile), the profile the
round fills (dshFillNewProfiles), and the effort pick (dshSetEffort). A
list read empty but written moments ago is reread after a beat, and the
write comes from the settled read; a still-empty one is dsh's own. The
model-set write says what it wrote where, so the next loss is findable in
minutes.

Ablation: with the reread out, TestDshSetWritesOnAListThatSettled,
TestDshFillNewProfilesWritesOnAListThatSettled and
TestDshSetEffortWritesOnAListThatSettled fail at "the user's entries are
gone" — the reporter's shape; with the log line out,
TestDshSetSaysWhatItWrote fails. A list that reads empty and stays empty
still takes the route (TestDshSetWritesThroughAStableEmptyList).

Run at upstream/main 2bb201162 + the #5782 gate rebased (e625dfc20) + this
commit, macOS 15 (darwin/arm64): the dsh family green, -race green;
internal/agent builds on linux, windows and darwin. A real Windows dsh
desktop mid-save is NOT-RUNNABLE here.

